***conformance tests***

> add conformance test scenarios here

***acceptance tests***

# unknown-func-id
`tests/a.plain` bound to `todo:delete-task` raises exactly `Plain syntax error: Test plain file 'tests/a.plain' binds to functionality 'todo:delete-task', which module 'todo' does not have.`.

# no-binding-keys
`tests/helper.plain` holding `***definitions***`, an empty line and `- ⟨Helper⟩ helps.` raises exactly `Plain syntax error: File 'tests/helper.plain' is under a tests folder but is not a test plain file: its frontmatter needs the keys `module:` and `func_id:`.`.

# invalid-frontmatter
`tests/broken.plain` holding `---`, `module: [`, `---` raises `PlainSyntaxError` holding `File 'tests/broken.plain' under a tests folder has invalid frontmatter`.

# file-errors-name-the-file
`tests/a.plain` bound to `todo:add-task` with only a conformance section raises `PlainSyntaxError` holding `Test plain file 'tests/a.plain' has no `***acceptance tests***`.

# not-a-text-file
`tests/bin.plain` holding the bytes 0x00 0xff 0xfe raises `PlainSyntaxError` holding `File 'tests/bin.plain' under a tests folder is not a text file.`.
